==============================================================================
VERDICT
==============================================================================
  drift with the sponge        3.8341%
  drift without it             0.0003%
  ratio                       12705.2x

  CAUSE (b): DESIGNED DISSIPATION. With the absorbing term removed the integrator
  conserves energy to within the gate, and switching it on reproduces the drift. The
  2% bar is therefore measuring the sponge, not the numerics, and it cannot be met by
  any run that uses an absorbing boundary -- which this instrument does by design,
  because a periodic box without one reflects the fountain's radiation back onto the
  ring it is trying to measure.

  This is NOT the spherical rebound run's situation. There the energy error was the
  integrator failing at 22-1817% with no dissipative term to blame, and burying the
  result was correct. Here the same symptom has a different cause, and the
  distinguishing measurement is the one above.

  RECOMMENDATION unchanged and now evidenced: re-scope gate (iii) to the physical
  region interior to the sponge, which is what it was written to protect. The parity
  test across n = +-1 is a RELATIVE comparison and a common dissipation cancels from
  it, so the fork's actual content survives either ruling.
